// A deliberately non-conforming requirement, to demonstrate that partiality is reported
// rather than silent. Taken verbatim from examples/req.ceps, already in this repository.
//
// It breaks INCOSE GtWR R19 (combinators "while", "unless"), R18 (two thoughts: a speed
// interlock and a crash override), and states a prohibition rather than a behaviour.
// It matches no accepted pattern, so no model element is generated for it - and the run
// says so, by requirement identifier.

REQ-101
The system shall not unlock the doors while vehicle speed is greater than 5 km/h
unless crash mode is active.
